-- `Ref` builds a mutable cell.  Generalizing `Ref x` would be unsound (write at
-- one type, read at another).  This binding must NOT generalize — using it at two
-- incompatible types must error.
--
-- `Ref` is excluded WITHOUT being named: `isCtorAppSpine` asks `lookupCtor` whether
-- the spine head is a declared data constructor, and `Ref` is an extern FUNCTION, so
-- it is never in that map.  This holds whether `Ref` is declared locally (as below)
-- or comes from the stdlib prelude — an `extern` never enters the ctor map either way.
-- The old test named "Ref" by hand and otherwise trusted the first character of the
-- name, which was issue 1150.
extern Ref : a -> Ref a
r = Ref (x => x)
-- Using r at two different function types in one tuple must produce a type error.
pair = ((r : Ref (Int -> Int)), (r : Ref (String -> String)))
